<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alvar Aalto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1898–1976</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alvar Aalto was a Finnish architect and designer, one of the leading figures of modern architecture. His buildings, such as the Paimio Sanatorium, the Villa Mairea and Finlandia Hall in Helsinki, combined modernist forms with natural materials and attention to human needs. His bent-plywood furniture and glassware, made by Artek and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iittala">Iittala</a>, helped establish the international reputation of Finnish design.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alvar-aalto.jpg" alt="Alvar Aalto" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alvar_Aalto1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
